From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] 0148: blueline watchdog: a hung kernel resets itself into
 recovery (bluewdt=N, bluewdt_mode=hw|sw|auto)

bluewdt=N (off by default) arms the SDM845 APSS watchdog (watchdog@17980000,
kpss layout: RST 0x4, EN 0x8, STS 0xc, BARK 0x10, BITE 0x14, 32768 Hz, 20
bits so N <= 31 s): logged and the log written to UFS before the first
read and the first write, registers logged as ABL left them, BITE = N s,
BARK = max (after the bite, unused), writes read back and the counter must
advance ~3277 ticks in 100 ms, else put back in reverse and (auto) the
software watchdog is used instead. A TIMER_CALL_LOCAL callout on the boot
CPU pets every second, only while a priority-80 thread (bluewdt_pri) ran
within bluewdt_stall s (default N/3): dead interrupts and a wedged
scheduler both stop the pets. First pet and every 60 s logged.

sw (bluewdt_mode=sw, or auto fallback): the same callout and thread are
heartbeats; a callout on the last CPU (bluewdt_cpu) resets when either is
N s silent: IMEM restart_reason = recovery, lock-free log write
(sweet_log_flush_emergency: takes the UFS host for that CPU, waits for a
command in flight), PSCI SYSTEM_RESET.

bluewdt_recovery=1: at arm time PON SOFT_RB_SPARE = 1 << 1 and IMEM
0x146bf65c = 0x77665502 (as 0127 does at reboot), so every later reset,
a bite included, goes to recovery.

Panic: SavePanicInfo spins for ever here (no iBoot panic region); before
that the ring is written to UFS without locks, then hw lets the bite come
(bluewdt_panic=reset, sw, or half-armed hw: PSCI reset at once). The
paniclog's unbuffered output (consdebug_putc_unbuffered, and consdebug_putc
with console output disabled) now goes into the ring too (after ios-flame
0098). bluereboot (0127): watchdog off right before its PSCI call, back on
if PSCI returns.

bluewdt_test=hang|sched|panic (bluewdt_test_after=S, default 20): interrupts
off and spin on the timer CPU / a priority-95 spinner bound to every CPU /
panic(), each after a synchronous log write.
---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/blueline_wdt.c b/bsd/dev/blueline_wdt.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..76d9e1b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/bsd/dev/blueline_wdt.c
@@ -0,0 +1,589 @@
+/*
+ * Pixel 3 (blueline) watchdog for the test loop (patch 0148): a hung
+ * kernel resets the phone by itself, and with slot B active that lands in
+ * LineageOS recovery, where tools/phonetest.sh pulls the log.
+ *
+ *   bluewdt=N              N seconds (off by default). hw: 2..31 (BITE_TIME
+ *                          is 20 bits of a 32768 Hz count), sw: 2..600
+ *   bluewdt_mode=auto      hw if the APSS watchdog takes our writes and
+ *                          counts, else sw (default); hw or sw to force one
+ *   bluewdt_recovery=1     at arm time, set the reboot reason to recovery the
+ *                          way 0127 does at reboot (PON SOFT_RB_SPARE 1 << 1
+ *                          and IMEM restart_reason 0x77665502), so a bite or
+ *                          any other reset goes to recovery (default 0)
+ *   bluewdt_stall=S        hw: the timer stops petting once the pet thread
+ *                          has not run for S s (default N / 3, at least 2)
+ *   bluewdt_pri=P          pet thread priority (default 80, the lowest
+ *                          kernel priority; 4 also catches user starvation)
+ *   bluewdt_cpu=C          sw: CPU of the checking timer (default the last)
+ *   bluewdt_panic=bite     on panic: write the log, then let the watchdog
+ *                          bite (default in hw); =reset: PSCI reset at once
+ *                          (always so in sw: the checker is halted then)
+ *   bluewdt_test=hang|sched|panic, bluewdt_test_after=S (default 20):
+ *                          hang = interrupts off and spin on the timer CPU,
+ *                          sched = a priority-95 spinner bound to every CPU
+ *                          (interrupts on, no thread below 95 runs),
+ *                          panic = panic(); each writes the log first
+ *
+ * hw: the SDM845 APSS watchdog (qcom,apss-wdt-sdm845 / qcom,kpss-wdt,
+ * watchdog@17980000; Linux qcom-wdt.c kpss layout, msm watchdog_v2.c WDT0_*):
+ * RST 0x04 (write 1 = pet), EN 0x08 (bit 0 enable, bit 1 unmasked bark
+ * interrupt), STS 0x0c (bit 0 expired, bits 20:1 count since the pet),
+ * BARK_TIME 0x10, BITE_TIME 0x14, in 32768 Hz ticks, 20 bits. The bite is
+ * handled by TZ, which resets the SoC. The bark (SPI 0) is not used:
+ * BARK_TIME is the maximum, after the bite. The block is read and logged
+ * before any write (each first access is logged and the log written to
+ * UFS first, so a faulting or hanging access names itself); writes are read
+ * back and the counter must advance, else auto falls back to sw.
+ *
+ * Petting: a timer callout (TIMER_CALL_LOCAL, interrupt context) on the boot
+ * CPU every second writes RST, but only while the pet thread (priority
+ * bluewdt_pri, also once a second) has run within bluewdt_stall s. Dead
+ * interrupts on that CPU stop the callout; a wedged scheduler stops the
+ * thread; either stops the pets. Nothing else pets.
+ *
+ * sw: the same callout and thread only record heartbeats; a second callout
+ * on bluewdt_cpu checks them every second and when either is N s old writes
+ * the console ring to UFS without locks (sweet_log_flush_emergency) and
+ * does 0127's reset: IMEM restart_reason = recovery, PSCI SYSTEM_RESET. It
+ * cannot take the PON (arbiter mutex) there; bluewdt_recovery=1 sets PON at
+ * arm time. sw cannot catch a hang that takes every CPU's interrupts.
+ *
+ * Panic (SavePanicInfo, osfmk/arm/model_dep.c): there is no iBoot panic
+ * region, so SavePanicInfo spins for ever. Before that, blueline_wdt_panic
+ * pets once, writes the ring to UFS, and in hw lets the bite come (<= N s);
+ * in sw, or with bluewdt_panic=reset, or when hw arming failed half-way,
+ * resets with PSCI itself.
+ *
+ * bluereboot (0127): the watchdog is switched off right before its PSCI
+ * call, and on again if PSCI returns.
+ */
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+#include <sys/param.h>
+#include <sys/systm.h>
+#include <sys/errno.h>
+#include <kern/clock.h>
+#include <kern/thread.h>
+#include <kern/sched_prim.h>
+#include <kern/cpu_number.h>
+#include <kern/timer_call.h>
+#include <mach/mach_time.h>
+#include <machine/machine_routines.h>
+#include <machine/atomic.h>
+#include <pexpert/pexpert.h>
+#include <libkern/libkern.h>
+#include <stdarg.h>
+
+extern vm_offset_t ml_io_map(vm_offset_t, vm_size_t);
+extern kern_return_t kernel_thread_start(thread_continue_t, void *, thread_t *);
+extern kern_return_t kernel_thread_start_priority(thread_continue_t, void *, integer_t, thread_t *);
+extern void thread_deallocate(thread_t);
+extern processor_t thread_bind(processor_t);
+extern processor_t cpu_to_processor(int);
+extern int hz;
+/* bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c */
+extern void sweet_log_append(const char *c, int size);
+extern int sweet_log_flush_now(void);
+extern int sweet_log_flush_emergency(void);
+/* bsd/dev/blueline_keys.c (0127) */
+extern int blueline_pon_set_reboot_reason(uint8_t reason, uint8_t *before, uint8_t *after);
+
+void blueline_wdt_start(void);
+void blueline_wdt_panic(void);
+void blueline_wdt_prepare_reset(const char *why);
+void blueline_wdt_suspend(void);
+void blueline_wdt_resume(void);
+
+#define WDT_PA                  0x17980000u     /* watchdog@17980000 */
+#define WDT_RST                 0x04u
+#define WDT_EN                  0x08u
+#define WDT_STS                 0x0cu
+#define WDT_BARK_TIME           0x10u
+#define WDT_BITE_TIME           0x14u
+#define WDT_HZ                  32768u
+#define WDT_MAX_TICKS           0xfffffu        /* 20 bits: 31.99 s */
+#define WDT_STS_COUNT(s)        (((s) >> 1) & 0xfffffu)
+
+#define BLUE_IMEM_PA            0x146bf000u     /* qcom,msm-imem@146bf000 */
+#define BLUE_IMEM_RESTART       0x65cu          /* restart_reason@65c */
+#define BLUE_IMEM_RECOVERY      0x77665502u
+#define PSCI_SYSTEM_RESET       0x84000009ull
+
+enum { BW_OFF, BW_HW, BW_SW };
+enum { BT_NONE, BT_HANG, BT_SCHED, BT_PANIC };
+
+static struct {
+	int mode;                               /* what runs */
+	bool wanted;                            /* bluewdt=N was given */
+	bool hw_touched;                        /* hw arming started (EN may be on) */
+	bool panic_reset;                       /* bluewdt_panic=reset */
+	uint32_t secs, stall, pri;
+	int pet_cpu, check_cpu;
+	int test;
+	uint32_t test_after;
+	vm_offset_t regs, imem;
+	uint64_t period_abs, secs_abs, stall_abs, t0;
+	timer_call_data_t pet_call, check_call;
+} bw;
+
+static uint64_t _Atomic bw_cb_beat, bw_thread_beat, bw_pets, bw_checks;
+static uint64_t _Atomic bw_first_pet;
+static bool _Atomic bw_suspended, bw_starved, bw_fired;
+static int bw_chan;
+
+static inline uint32_t
+wdt_rd(uint32_t off)
+{
+	return *(volatile uint32_t *)(bw.regs + off);
+}
+
+static inline void
+wdt_wr(uint32_t off, uint32_t v)
+{
+	*(volatile uint32_t *)(bw.regs + off) = v;
+	__asm__ volatile ("dsb sy" ::: "memory");
+}
+
+static uint64_t
+bw_ms(uint64_t abs)
+{
+	uint64_t ns;
+	absolutetime_to_nanoseconds(abs, &ns);
+	return ns / NSEC_PER_MSEC;
+}
+
+static uint64_t
+bw_abs(uint64_t secs)
+{
+	uint64_t abs;
+	nanoseconds_to_absolutetime(secs * NSEC_PER_SEC, &abs);
+	return abs;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Straight into the console ring (sweet_ufs.c), for interrupt and panic
+ * context: printf there only reaches the console's own buffer, which is
+ * drained later by threads that may never run again.
+ */
+static void __printflike(1, 2)
+bw_log_direct(const char *fmt, ...)
+{
+	char line[200];
+	va_list ap;
+	va_start(ap, fmt);
+	int n = vsnprintf(line, sizeof(line), fmt, ap);
+	va_end(ap);
+	if (n > 0) {
+		sweet_log_append(line, MIN(n, (int)sizeof(line) - 1));
+	}
+}
+
+static void
+bw_bind(int cpu)
+{
+	processor_t p = cpu_to_processor(cpu);
+	if (p != PROCESSOR_NULL) {
+		(void)thread_bind(p);
+		thread_block(THREAD_CONTINUE_NULL);     /* migrate to the bound core */
+	}
+}
+
+static void
+bw_sleep(uint32_t secs)
+{
+	(void)tsleep(&bw_chan, PZERO, "bluewdt", (int)secs * hz);
+}
+
+/* 0127's reset, without locks: IMEM cookie, log, PSCI. Returns only on failure. */
+static void
+bw_reset_now(const char *why)
+{
+	if (bw.imem) {
+		*(volatile uint32_t *)(bw.imem + BLUE_IMEM_RESTART) = BLUE_IMEM_RECOVERY;
+		__asm__ volatile ("dsb sy" ::: "memory");
+	}
+	bw_log_direct("BLUELINE WDT: %s: IMEM restart_reason %s 0x%08x, log to UFS, PSCI SYSTEM_RESET (cpu %d)\n",
+	    why, bw.imem ? "=" : "unmapped", BLUE_IMEM_RECOVERY, cpu_number());
+	int error = sweet_log_flush_emergency();
+	register uint64_t x0 __asm__("x0") = PSCI_SYSTEM_RESET;
+	__asm__ volatile ("smc #0" : "+r"(x0) : :
+	    "x1", "x2", "x3", "x4", "x5", "x6", "x7", "x8", "x9", "x10", "x11",
+	    "x12", "x13", "x14", "x15", "x16", "x17", "cc", "memory");
+	bw_log_direct("BLUELINE WDT: did not reset (log write %d, PSCI %d)\n", error, (int)(int32_t)x0);
+}
+
+/* Interrupt context, on bw.pet_cpu, every second. */
+static void
+bw_pet_call(__unused timer_call_param_t p0, __unused timer_call_param_t p1)
+{
+	uint64_t now = mach_absolute_time();
+
+	os_atomic_store(&bw_cb_beat, now, relaxed);
+	if (bw.mode == BW_HW && !os_atomic_load(&bw_suspended, relaxed)) {
+		uint64_t tb = os_atomic_load(&bw_thread_beat, relaxed);
+		if (now - tb <= bw.stall_abs) {
+			wdt_wr(WDT_RST, 1);
+			if (os_atomic_inc_orig(&bw_pets, relaxed) == 0) {
+				os_atomic_store(&bw_first_pet, now, relaxed);
+			}
+			os_atomic_store(&bw_starved, false, relaxed);
+		} else if (!os_atomic_xchg(&bw_starved, true, relaxed)) {
+			bw_log_direct("BLUELINE WDT: pet thread silent for %llu ms: no more pets, bite in <= %u s\n",
+			    bw_ms(now - tb), bw.secs);
+		}
+	}
+	timer_call_enter(&bw.pet_call, now + bw.period_abs, TIMER_CALL_SYS_CRITICAL | TIMER_CALL_LOCAL);
+}
+
+/* sw: interrupt context, on bw.check_cpu, every second. */
+static void
+bw_check_call(__unused timer_call_param_t p0, __unused timer_call_param_t p1)
+{
+	uint64_t now = mach_absolute_time();
+
+	os_atomic_inc(&bw_checks, relaxed);
+	if (!os_atomic_load(&bw_suspended, relaxed)) {
+		uint64_t cb = now - os_atomic_load(&bw_cb_beat, relaxed);
+		uint64_t tb = now - os_atomic_load(&bw_thread_beat, relaxed);
+		if ((cb > bw.secs_abs || tb > bw.secs_abs) && !os_atomic_xchg(&bw_fired, true, relaxed)) {
+			bw_log_direct("BLUELINE WDT: software watchdog: timer on cpu%d silent %llu ms, pet thread %llu ms\n",
+			    bw.pet_cpu, bw_ms(cb), bw_ms(tb));
+			bw_reset_now("software watchdog");
+			return;
+		}
+	}
+	timer_call_enter(&bw.check_call, now + bw.period_abs, TIMER_CALL_SYS_CRITICAL | TIMER_CALL_LOCAL);
+}
+
+__dead2 static void
+bw_spin_thread(void *arg, __unused wait_result_t wr)
+{
+	bw_bind((int)(uintptr_t)arg);
+	for (;;) {
+		__asm__ volatile ("" ::: "memory");
+	}
+}
+
+static void
+bw_test_thread(__unused void *arg, __unused wait_result_t wr)
+{
+	bw_sleep(bw.test_after);
+	switch (bw.test) {
+	case BT_HANG:
+		bw_bind(bw.pet_cpu);
+		printf("BLUELINE WDT TEST: hang: interrupts off on cpu%d (the timer's), spinning; "
+		    "expect a reset within %u s\n", cpu_number(), bw.secs + 2);
+		(void)sweet_log_flush_now();
+		(void)ml_set_interrupts_enabled(FALSE);
+		for (;;) {
+			__asm__ volatile ("" ::: "memory");
+		}
+	case BT_SCHED: {
+		unsigned n = ml_get_cpu_count();
+		printf("BLUELINE WDT TEST: sched: a priority-95 spinner on each of %u CPUs; "
+		    "expect a reset within %u s\n", n, bw.mode == BW_HW ? bw.stall + bw.secs + 2 : bw.secs + 2);
+		(void)sweet_log_flush_now();
+		for (unsigned c = 0; c < n; c++) {
+			thread_t t;
+			if (kernel_thread_start_priority(bw_spin_thread, (void *)(uintptr_t)c, 95, &t) == KERN_SUCCESS) {
+				thread_deallocate(t);
+			}
+		}
+		return;
+	}
+	case BT_PANIC:
+		printf("BLUELINE WDT TEST: panic on purpose\n");
+		(void)sweet_log_flush_now();
+		panic("BLUELINE WDT TEST: bluewdt_test=panic");
+	default:
+		return;
+	}
+}
+
+__dead2 static void
+bw_thread(__unused void *arg, __unused wait_result_t wr)
+{
+	/* Arm the timer callouts on their CPUs: TIMER_CALL_LOCAL keeps them there. */
+	os_atomic_store(&bw_thread_beat, mach_absolute_time(), relaxed);
+	os_atomic_store(&bw_cb_beat, mach_absolute_time(), relaxed);
+	processor_t prev = PROCESSOR_NULL;
+	if (cpu_to_processor(bw.pet_cpu) != PROCESSOR_NULL) {
+		prev = thread_bind(cpu_to_processor(bw.pet_cpu));
+		thread_block(THREAD_CONTINUE_NULL);
+	}
+	int pet_on = cpu_number();
+	timer_call_enter(&bw.pet_call, mach_absolute_time() + bw.period_abs / 4,
+	    TIMER_CALL_SYS_CRITICAL | TIMER_CALL_LOCAL);
+	int check_on = -1;
+	if (bw.mode == BW_SW) {
+		bw_bind(bw.check_cpu);
+		check_on = cpu_number();
+		timer_call_enter(&bw.check_call, mach_absolute_time() + bw.period_abs,
+		    TIMER_CALL_SYS_CRITICAL | TIMER_CALL_LOCAL);
+	}
+	(void)thread_bind(prev);
+	thread_block(THREAD_CONTINUE_NULL);
+	if (check_on >= 0) {
+		printf("BLUELINE WDT: sw: timer on cpu%d, checker on cpu%d%s, pet thread priority %u\n",
+		    pet_on, check_on, check_on == pet_on ? " (same CPU: an interrupts-off hang there is missed)" : "",
+		    bw.pri);
+	} else {
+		printf("BLUELINE WDT: hw: timer on cpu%d, pet thread priority %u\n", pet_on, bw.pri);
+	}
+
+	bool first = false;
+	uint64_t next_report = mach_absolute_time() + bw_abs(60);
+	for (;;) {
+		uint64_t now = mach_absolute_time();
+		os_atomic_store(&bw_thread_beat, now, relaxed);
+		if (bw.mode == BW_HW && !first && os_atomic_load(&bw_pets, relaxed) != 0) {
+			first = true;
+			printf("BLUELINE WDT: first pet at %llu ms after arming (STS 0x%x)\n",
+			    bw_ms(os_atomic_load(&bw_first_pet, relaxed) - bw.t0), wdt_rd(WDT_STS));
+		}
+		if (now >= next_report) {
+			next_report += bw_abs(60);
+			uint64_t cb = now - os_atomic_load(&bw_cb_beat, relaxed);
+			if (bw.mode == BW_HW) {
+				uint32_t sts = wdt_rd(WDT_STS);
+				printf("BLUELINE WDT: hw alive %llu s: %llu pets, timer %llu ms ago, count %u ticks "
+				    "(%u ms) since the pet, EN 0x%x%s\n", bw_ms(now - bw.t0) / 1000,
+				    os_atomic_load(&bw_pets, relaxed), bw_ms(cb), WDT_STS_COUNT(sts),
+				    WDT_STS_COUNT(sts) * 1000u / WDT_HZ, wdt_rd(WDT_EN),
+				    os_atomic_load(&bw_suspended, relaxed) ? " (suspended)" : "");
+			} else {
+				printf("BLUELINE WDT: sw alive %llu s: %llu checks, timer %llu ms ago\n",
+				    bw_ms(now - bw.t0) / 1000, os_atomic_load(&bw_checks, relaxed), bw_ms(cb));
+			}
+		}
+		bw_sleep(1);
+	}
+}
+
+/*
+ * Try the APSS watchdog. Every first access is logged and the log written
+ * to UFS before it. On failure the registers are put back in reverse.
+ */
+static bool
+bw_hw_arm(void)
+{
+	printf("BLUELINE WDT: about to map and read the APSS watchdog at 0x%x (EN, STS, BARK, BITE)\n", WDT_PA);
+	(void)sweet_log_flush_now();
+	bw.regs = ml_io_map(WDT_PA, 0x1000);
+	if (!bw.regs) {
+		printf("BLUELINE WDT: mapping failed\n");
+		return false;
+	}
+	uint32_t en0 = wdt_rd(WDT_EN), sts0 = wdt_rd(WDT_STS);
+	uint32_t bark0 = wdt_rd(WDT_BARK_TIME), bite0 = wdt_rd(WDT_BITE_TIME);
+	printf("BLUELINE WDT: as ABL left it: EN 0x%x (%s), STS 0x%x (expired bit %u, count %u = %u ms), "
+	    "BARK 0x%x (%u ms), BITE 0x%x (%u ms)\n", en0, (en0 & 1) ? "running" : "off", sts0, sts0 & 1u,
+	    WDT_STS_COUNT(sts0), WDT_STS_COUNT(sts0) * 1000u / WDT_HZ, bark0, bark0 * 1000u / WDT_HZ,
+	    bite0, bite0 * 1000u / WDT_HZ);
+
+	uint32_t ticks = bw.secs * WDT_HZ;
+	printf("BLUELINE WDT: about to write it: EN 0, pet, BARK 0x%x, BITE 0x%x, EN 1\n", WDT_MAX_TICKS, ticks);
+	(void)sweet_log_flush_now();
+	bw.hw_touched = true;
+	wdt_wr(WDT_EN, 0);
+	wdt_wr(WDT_RST, 1);
+	wdt_wr(WDT_BARK_TIME, WDT_MAX_TICKS);   /* after the bite: never seen */
+	wdt_wr(WDT_BITE_TIME, ticks);
+	uint32_t bark = wdt_rd(WDT_BARK_TIME), bite = wdt_rd(WDT_BITE_TIME);
+	const char *why = NULL;
+	uint32_t en = 0, c0 = 0, c1 = 0;
+	if (bark != WDT_MAX_TICKS || bite != ticks) {
+		why = "BARK/BITE writes ignored (secure-only?)";
+	} else {
+		wdt_wr(WDT_EN, 1);
+		en = wdt_rd(WDT_EN);
+		c0 = WDT_STS_COUNT(wdt_rd(WDT_STS));
+		delay(100 * 1000);
+		c1 = WDT_STS_COUNT(wdt_rd(WDT_STS));
+		wdt_wr(WDT_RST, 1);
+		if (!(en & 1)) {
+			why = "EN write ignored";
+		} else if (c1 <= c0 || c1 - c0 < 1000 || c1 - c0 > 10000) {
+			why = "counter does not advance ~3277 ticks in 100 ms";
+		}
+	}
+	if (why) {
+		/* undo, in reverse */
+		wdt_wr(WDT_EN, 0);
+		wdt_wr(WDT_BITE_TIME, bite0);
+		wdt_wr(WDT_BARK_TIME, bark0);
+		wdt_wr(WDT_RST, 1);
+		wdt_wr(WDT_EN, en0);
+		bw.hw_touched = (wdt_rd(WDT_EN) & 1) != 0;
+		printf("BLUELINE WDT: hw unusable: %s (BARK 0x%x BITE 0x%x EN 0x%x, count %u -> %u); "
+		    "registers put back, EN now 0x%x\n", why, bark, bite, en, c0, c1, wdt_rd(WDT_EN));
+		return false;
+	}
+	printf("BLUELINE WDT: hw armed: bite after %u s without a pet (BITE 0x%x, BARK 0x%x unused), "
+	    "count %u -> %u in 100 ms; pets only while the pet thread ran within %u s\n",
+	    bw.secs, bite, bark, c0, c1, bw.stall);
+	return true;
+}
+
+void
+blueline_wdt_start(void)
+{
+	char mode[8] = "auto", test[8] = "", panicm[8] = "bite";
+	uint32_t recovery = 0;
+	thread_t thread;
+
+	if (!PE_parse_boot_argn("bluewdt", &bw.secs, sizeof(bw.secs)) || bw.secs == 0) {
+		return;
+	}
+	bw.wanted = true;
+	(void)PE_parse_boot_arg_str("bluewdt_mode", mode, sizeof(mode));
+	(void)PE_parse_boot_arg_str("bluewdt_test", test, sizeof(test));
+	(void)PE_parse_boot_arg_str("bluewdt_panic", panicm, sizeof(panicm));
+	(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("bluewdt_recovery", &recovery, sizeof(recovery));
+	bw.test_after = 20;
+	(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("bluewdt_test_after", &bw.test_after, sizeof(bw.test_after));
+	bw.pri = 80;
+	(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("bluewdt_pri", &bw.pri, sizeof(bw.pri));
+	bw.pri = MAX(1u, MIN(bw.pri, 95u));
+	unsigned ncpu = ml_get_cpu_count();
+	bw.pet_cpu = ml_get_boot_cpu_number();
+	bw.check_cpu = (int)ncpu - 1;
+	(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("bluewdt_cpu", &bw.check_cpu, sizeof(bw.check_cpu));
+	if (bw.check_cpu < 0 || (unsigned)bw.check_cpu >= ncpu) {
+		bw.check_cpu = (int)ncpu - 1;
+	}
+	bw.panic_reset = !strcmp(panicm, "reset");
+	bw.test = !strcmp(test, "hang") ? BT_HANG : !strcmp(test, "sched") ? BT_SCHED :
+	    !strcmp(test, "panic") ? BT_PANIC : BT_NONE;
+
+	bool try_hw = strcmp(mode, "sw") != 0, allow_sw = strcmp(mode, "hw") != 0;
+	if (strcmp(mode, "hw") && strcmp(mode, "sw") && strcmp(mode, "auto")) {
+		printf("BLUELINE WDT: bluewdt_mode=%s is not hw|sw|auto; using auto\n", mode);
+	}
+	printf("BLUELINE WDT: bluewdt=%u mode %s%s%s%s\n", bw.secs, mode,
+	    recovery ? ", reason recovery from now" : "", bw.test ? ", test " : "", bw.test ? test : "");
+
+	bw.imem = ml_io_map(BLUE_IMEM_PA, 0x1000);
+	if (recovery) {
+		uint8_t before = 0, after = 0;
+		int pon = blueline_pon_set_reboot_reason(1, &before, &after);
+		if (bw.imem) {
+			*(volatile uint32_t *)(bw.imem + BLUE_IMEM_RESTART) = BLUE_IMEM_RECOVERY;
+			__asm__ volatile ("dsb sy" ::: "memory");
+		}
+		printf("BLUELINE WDT: reboot reason recovery now: PON SOFT_RB_SPARE 0x%02x -> 0x%02x (%d), "
+		    "IMEM restart_reason %s 0x%08x; every reset from here goes to recovery\n",
+		    before, after, pon, bw.imem ? "=" : "unmapped", BLUE_IMEM_RECOVERY);
+	}
+
+	bw.stall = MAX(2u, bw.secs / 3);
+	(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("bluewdt_stall", &bw.stall, sizeof(bw.stall));
+	bw.period_abs = bw_abs(1);
+	timer_call_setup(&bw.pet_call, bw_pet_call, NULL);
+	timer_call_setup(&bw.check_call, bw_check_call, NULL);
+
+	uint32_t asked = bw.secs;
+	if (try_hw) {
+		bw.secs = MAX(2u, MIN(bw.secs, WDT_MAX_TICKS / WDT_HZ));
+		if (bw.secs != asked) {
+			printf("BLUELINE WDT: hw bite time %u s -> %u s (2..31)\n", asked, bw.secs);
+		}
+		bw.stall = MAX(1u, MIN(bw.stall, bw.secs - 1));
+		/* The thread's beat must be fresh before EN goes on. */
+		os_atomic_store(&bw_thread_beat, mach_absolute_time(), relaxed);
+		if (bw_hw_arm()) {
+			bw.mode = BW_HW;
+		}
+	}
+	if (bw.mode == BW_OFF && allow_sw) {
+		bw.secs = MAX(2u, MIN(asked, 600u));
+		bw.mode = BW_SW;
+		printf("BLUELINE WDT: sw: reset when the timer on cpu%d or the pet thread is silent %u s\n",
+		    bw.pet_cpu, bw.secs);
+	}
+	if (bw.mode == BW_OFF) {
+		printf("BLUELINE WDT: off (hw unusable, bluewdt_mode=hw)\n");
+		return;
+	}
+	bw.secs_abs = bw_abs(bw.secs);
+	bw.stall_abs = bw_abs(bw.stall);
+	bw.t0 = mach_absolute_time();
+	if (kernel_thread_start_priority(bw_thread, NULL, (integer_t)bw.pri, &thread) == KERN_SUCCESS) {
+		thread_deallocate(thread);
+	} else {
+		printf("BLUELINE WDT: no pet thread: %s\n", bw.mode == BW_HW ? "the watchdog will bite" : "off");
+	}
+	if (bw.test && kernel_thread_start(bw_test_thread, NULL, &thread) == KERN_SUCCESS) {
+		printf("BLUELINE WDT TEST: %s in %u s\n", test, bw.test_after);
+		thread_deallocate(thread);
+	}
+}
+
+/*
+ * From SavePanicInfo, interrupts off, the other CPUs halted. Writes the
+ * console ring to UFS, then lets the hw watchdog bite or resets now.
+ */
+void
+blueline_wdt_panic(void)
+{
+	static bool once;
+
+	if (!bw.wanted || once) {
+		return;
+	}
+	once = true;
+	bool bite = bw.mode == BW_HW && !bw.panic_reset && !os_atomic_load(&bw_suspended, relaxed);
+	if (bw.mode == BW_HW) {
+		wdt_wr(WDT_RST, 1);                     /* a whole period for the log write */
+	}
+	bw_log_direct("BLUELINE WDT: panic on cpu%d: writing the log to UFS, then %s\n", cpu_number(),
+	    bite ? "the watchdog bites" : "PSCI reset");
+	int error = sweet_log_flush_emergency();
+	if (bite) {
+		bw_log_direct("BLUELINE WDT: panic log written (%d); bite in <= %u s\n", error, bw.secs);
+		(void)sweet_log_flush_emergency();
+		return;
+	}
+	if (bw.hw_touched && bw.mode != BW_HW && bw.regs) {
+		wdt_wr(WDT_RST, 1);                     /* half-armed hw: keep it out of the reset path */
+	}
+	bw_reset_now("panic");
+}
+
+/* bluereboot (0127): one line before its log write, then off right before PSCI. */
+void
+blueline_wdt_prepare_reset(const char *why)
+{
+	if (bw.mode != BW_OFF) {
+		printf("BLUELINE WDT: %s: watchdog off right before the PSCI reset\n", why);
+	}
+}
+
+void
+blueline_wdt_suspend(void)
+{
+	if (bw.mode == BW_OFF) {
+		return;
+	}
+	os_atomic_store(&bw_suspended, true, relaxed);
+	if (bw.mode == BW_HW) {
+		wdt_wr(WDT_EN, 0);
+	}
+}
+
+void
+blueline_wdt_resume(void)
+{
+	if (bw.mode == BW_OFF) {
+		return;
+	}
+	os_atomic_store(&bw_thread_beat, mach_absolute_time(), relaxed);
+	os_atomic_store(&bw_cb_beat, mach_absolute_time(), relaxed);
+	if (bw.mode == BW_HW) {
+		wdt_wr(WDT_RST, 1);
+		wdt_wr(WDT_EN, 1);
+	}
+	os_atomic_store(&bw_suspended, false, relaxed);
+	printf("BLUELINE WDT: back on (EN 0x%x)\n", bw.mode == BW_HW ? wdt_rd(WDT_EN) : 0);
+}
